  "body": "## What changed\n\n`camcraft_app::nc_sim` simulates an external NC program against the selected setup. Its entry points are `simulate_nc`, `simulate_nc_text`, `unmapped_tools` and `play_seed`. The runner reads the document and changes nothing. It is not an undoable command. The MCP tool and CLI command are follow-up #2220.\n\nThe tool map reads an explicit `T -> tool` mapping first, then document tool numbers, then numbered `.camtools` rows. It reports each unmapped number and refuses simulation if any number lacks cutter geometry. Only supported milling cutters pass the map.\n\nThe runner transforms program coordinates into world millimetres with `world = origin + sign * program_mm`. It reads the setup WCS or caller origins for `G54`..`G59`. A single negated in-plane axis reverses arc sense. An unstated work offset or turned setup WCS is refused.\n\nThe runner cuts the setup stock with the column engine and measures deviation against the target. It checks target gouges, fixture collisions and machine limits. Findings name their 1-based NC line. Machine checks include travel, feed, spindle speed, tool size and changer capacity. `play_seed` builds a `PlaySeed` for `FieldPlay` playback. Missing stock is refused by name.\n\n`camcraft-app` now depends on `camcraft-gcode`. The workspace entry returns because the app uses it. `docs/decisions/2218-nc-sim-runner.md` records this dependency and the review-fix decisions.\n\n## Latest review findings addressed\n\n1. **Initial motion.** The caller must confirm the parser's actual start with `NcSimOptions::initial_position_known`. The runner preserves the complete first move. Unknown starts refuse simulation and playback for straight moves and arcs. It does not collapse a traverse between clear endpoints.\n2. **Unsupported taper tips.** The shared tool-resolution guard applies `taper::is_unread_tip` to explicit, document and library sources. It refuses sane flat and ball taper tips instead of checking them as sharp cones.\n3. **Mesh fidelity.** One preparation guard checks the selected stock, target and fixtures. Unknown fidelity refuses simulation and playback. Reduced stock or target fidelity tightens the tolerance by the maximum excess. The guard uses the strict law because the checks include shanks and holders. An explicit tolerance cannot restore an exhausted fidelity budget. Known coarse fixture boxes retain their chord growth. Target and fixture overrides replace their corresponding document inputs. Playback receives the same adjusted tolerance.\n\n## Pin proof\n\nThe tests join the existing `stock_sim_document` binary. Original integration pins are in `nc_program.rs`; review pins are in `stock_sim_document/nc_safety.rs`. No new test binary was added.\n\nEach of these four mutations caused behavioral failures. Each fix was then restored. The final restored suite passed with **29 tests and 0 failures**.\n\n| Mutation | Failing pins in `nc_program::safety` |\n|---|---|\n| Restore first-move collapse | `nc_first_rapid_crossing_fixture_is_checked_with_clear_endpoints`; `nc_first_feed_crossing_target_is_checked_with_clear_endpoints` |\n| Remove unknown-start guard | `nc_unknown_start_refuses_straights_and_arcs_in_simulation_and_playback` |\n| Remove taper-tip guard | `nc_flat_and_ball_taper_tips_are_refused_from_every_tool_source` |\n| Remove shared fidelity guard | All six fidelity pins below |\n\nThe fidelity mutation failed these pins:\n\n- `nc_reduced_target_tightens_simulation_and_playback_even_with_explicit_tolerance`\n- `nc_reduced_stock_tightens_simulation_and_playback_without_document_target`\n- `nc_unknown_target_and_fixture_refuse_simulation_and_playback_with_explicit_tolerance`\n- `nc_unknown_stock_refuses_even_when_target_and_fixtures_are_overridden`\n- `nc_unverifiable_reduced_target_cannot_be_bypassed_by_a_large_tolerance`\n- `nc_legacy_stock_with_a_missing_source_refuses_simulation_and_playback`\n\n## Final-head validation\n\nHead: `7b01e1ebebe7194501a4b501cafcaf14d5b9693d`.\nQuick base: `upstream/main` at `6898b02ea3195e9124e6113afd6ab3cee38d0c50`.\nHeavy base, fetched between gates: `upstream/main` at `2394b5ad1efc573b7b99a898a02cc4225b4d9893`.\n\n- `env RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -j12 -p camcraft-app --test stock_sim_document -- --test-threads=12`: 29 passed, 0 failed after mutation restoration.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 1014 steps, 1013 passed and one `wire_post` environment failure, 0 stalls, 27.8 minutes. The failed-step rerun passed one step and 37 tests in 19 seconds. It used `TMPDIR=/tmp/camcraft-4470-tests.THHWZJ` and `--failed gate-logs/quick-20261128-000720`. All 1014 steps have passing coverage. No source changed between runs. Stale seeded metadata was repaired with package-specific target cleanup before the completed full run; no code fix was needed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed. The final quick gate also passed all-crate clippy.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 125 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 42.6 minutes. Three declared known-failure steps for #1950 failed as expected and were accepted by the gate: motion `the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock`, motion `the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note`, and app `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level`. These are expected failures, not newly passing tests.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 11 twins, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 4.0 minutes.\n- Catalog suites passed: `app suites: example_catalog`, `app suites: example_catalog_adaptive`, `app suites: example_catalog_edge_work`. `app heavy: example_catalog` also passed in 9 seconds.\n- UI screenshots: not applicable. No UI file changed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The three ordinary catalog suites and the reached heavy catalog suite passed. No `.nc`, `.cl` or catalog file changed. The committed worktree is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Klartext input through `parse_klartext`.\n- Part alignment and a multi-setup document. The runner reads one caller-selected setup.\n- `G28`/`G53` reference moves through `ParseOptions::references`.\n- A mounted `.mch` read from the document. The machine pin supplies an override; document loading uses `machine::of_setup`.\n- Graph update: `graphify` is absent from `PATH`. No package was installed.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Simulate an external G-code program against the setup stock, target model, fixtures and machine, with each finding on its NC line (`app::nc_sim`).\n\nFixes #2218\n",
